# Project: TravelAgency
Personal pet project. Repo and wiki are PUBLIC: anything pushed is visible forever.
## Facts
- Repo `PlutoGr/TravelAgency`; wiki = separate repo `TravelAgency.wiki.git`, branch `master`, push = publish.
- Board: GitHub Project (private) «PlutoGr/projects/2». Columns Очередь, В работе, На ревью, Готово.
- Stack: .NET 10 microservices (`src/Services`), gateway, React/TS frontend (`src/Frontend/travel-agency-frontend`, vitest). Tests: `*.UnitTests`, `*.IntegrationTests` (Testcontainers). Follow neighbouring code.
- Single environment: dev (Staging), behind basic auth, self-signed cert. Address and credentials: not in the repo; dev access and server facts come from the lead. Smoke on dev = login, catalog, booking.
- Merge to `main` = automatic deploy to dev («Deploy to dev»). Green CI = `.NET сборка и тесты`, `Фронтенд сборка и тесты`, `gitleaks`.
- Secret values live only on the server `.env`, GitHub Secrets (env `dev`), local `dotnet user-secrets`. Never in the repo.
- Repo wins over any doc; `.cursor/rules/project-github-formats.mdc` and `.github/pull_request_template.md` win on format conflicts.
- Normative and product documentation lives only in `.cursor/` (rules/agents), `AGENTS.md`, and the GitHub wiki (`Home`, `Doc-`, `Plan-`, `Epic-`, `Feature-`). Do not keep a repo `docs/` (or similar) tree for conventions, product TZ, or one-off artifacts. Do not commit agent skill manifests (`skills-lock.json`, cloned skill packs, Refero/design skill locks): those belong in the owner global Cursor/agent setup, not this project repo.
## Roles (overrides playbook role names)
| Role | Who | Zone |
|---|---|---|
| Lead | whoever holds the lead role (orchestrator) | Owner channel, triage, board, merges, cloud launches, server, audit, Doc- gaps; also executes architect duties below |
| Architect / escalated review | lead via cloud agent (brief `.cursor/agents/architect.md`) | Architecture, ADR, labels, task split; review only on step-6 escalation |
| Developer | cloud agent | App code + tests via PR (`playbook-cloud-agents.mdc`) |
| Tester | lead or cloud agent | Test cases / automated tests via cloud; acceptance on dev = lead (dev access) |
| DevOps | lead (+ cloud for CI/Docker files) | CI, Docker, nginx, deploy, server; PR security comments = automations |
| Analyst | lead via cloud agent | Wiki Epic/Feature sections, requirements, acceptance criteria |
- Single orchestrator: the lead. Do not hand project work to another teammate chat (handoff risk).
- Persistent TA chat bots are retired; do not route new work through team group chats.
## Priorities
Product themes (coarse product focus; not the Очередь number field): 1. Bugs and UX. 2. Profiles. 3. Chat. 4. Aggregation. Lead orders within this; theme-order changes need the owner.
Board queue numbers (field «Приоритет», 1 = next): `project-github-formats.mdc` «Queue priority» (Roadmap → epic sequence/parallel sets → task priorities; lead sets the field; refresh on demand, weekly audit, and each new issue).
## Parallel work
- Features under one epic may run in parallel. Merge one PR at a time; work may continue: per stream 1 active item + at most 1 waiting.
- Next issue only if it touches no files/endpoints/migrations of an open PR, does not depend on an unmerged PR, and its criteria are final. Branch from fresh `main`.
- Any doubt about overlap: wait or escalate to the architect. After the previous merge, update the branch before review.
- Returns first (acceptance bug, review changes, new analysis for an item in flight) over new work.
## Merge order
- Merger: the lead. Before merge: green CI, Cursor Automations finished (`project-cursor-automations.mdc`), a finished reply on every open finding (`playbook-step-06-review.mdc`), and step 6 escalation when it triggers. If the owner already put the task in work or explicitly authorized that work and the PR matches that scope, merge without a separate yes and notify after merge. Ask before merge only for the cases in `00-core.mdc`. Next merge only after «Deploy to dev» is green.
- Do not require a separate architect pass on every small/routine PR when automations are clean; when step 6 escalation triggers, the lead launches a cloud agent with `.cursor/agents/architect.md` (or reviews trivial diffs itself) and posts the verdict.
- Dependabot npm and NuGet (minor, patch, and major, including vitest, eslint, jsdom, node): automations plus the dependency rule in `playbook-git-pr.mdc` (green CI and no owner clarification, then notify what was merged; otherwise do not merge). docker and github-actions (including grouped updates that may contain majors): owner «да» before merge, because merge deploys to dev with SSH secrets and CI does not validate image or action supply chain the way app build and tests do.
- Docs-with-code = the matching wiki `Doc-` page (or a Doc- gap issue opened from the after-merge automation).
- Temporary dumps on dev allowed if deleted after the check.
## Cloud agents (project specifics; method in `playbook-cloud-agents.mdc`)
- Cloud-first (Oct 28, 2026, unified subscription): use a cloud agent for any TravelAgency repo task where a short brief is enough and the lead should not keep the digests in chat memory (code, tests, analysis, architecture text, CI/Docker edits, deep review). Lead stays the controller: triage, brief, review the result, `reply` for fixes, cancel orphans, coordinate in-flight agents (`playbook-cloud-agents.mdc` «Orchestrator loop»), then merge gates, board, wiki publish, server/dev acceptance.
- Developer: all code via a cloud agent, including bugs and tiny fixes. In chat only work needing live dev/server access or chat history.
- Analyst / architecture text: cloud agent returns ready Russian wiki/issue text; lead publishes.
- Tester: acceptance on dev stays with whoever has dev access (lead); automated tests and test-case drafts via a cloud agent when an issue needs them.
- DevOps: server stays with the lead; a cloud agent may edit workflows or Dockerfiles, lead checks the diff.
- Launch: repo `https://github.com/PlutoGr/TravelAgency`, title with the issue number, branch `type/NN-short-english-slug` (`playbook-git-pr.mdc` «Branch naming»).
- Gates after a cloud agent: strip Cursor PR markers, then merge order above. Cloud agents never touch the wiki, the board or merges.
- No usage-mode matrix; no scheduled limits refresh.
